# 🥉 Solution 3: **BFS (Queue-based)** — Iterative Breadth-First

### 💡 Logic
- Use queue to traverse graph level by level.
- Clone nodes as you visit.
- Easy to visualize.

### ✅ Code
```c
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <stdbool.h>

struct Node {
    int val;
    int numNeighbors;
    struct Node** neighbors;
};

// Simple queue
struct Node* queue[101];
int front = 0, rear = 0;

void enqueue(struct Node* n) { queue[rear++] = n; }
struct Node* dequeue() { return queue[front++]; }
bool isEmpty() { return front == rear; }

struct Node* cloneGraph(struct Node* s) {
    if (s == NULL) return NULL;

    struct Node* visited[101] = {NULL};

    // Clone the start node
    struct Node* cloneStart = (struct Node*)malloc(sizeof(struct Node));
    cloneStart->val = s->val;
    cloneStart->numNeighbors = s->numNeighbors;
    cloneStart->neighbors = (struct Node**)malloc(sizeof(struct Node*) * s->numNeighbors);
    visited[s->val] = cloneStart;

    enqueue(s);

    while (!isEmpty()) {
        struct Node* cur = dequeue();

        for (int i = 0; i < cur->numNeighbors; i++) {
            struct Node* neighbor = cur->neighbors[i];

            // If not cloned, create it
            if (visited[neighbor->val] == NULL) {
                struct Node* newNode = (struct Node*)malloc(sizeof(struct Node));
                newNode->val = neighbor->val;
                newNode->numNeighbors = neighbor->numNeighbors;
                newNode->neighbors = (struct Node**)malloc(sizeof(struct Node*) * neighbor->numNeighbors);
                visited[neighbor->val] = newNode;
                enqueue(neighbor);
            }
        }
    }

    // Connect cloned neighbors
    for (int i = 1; i <= 100; i++) {
        if (visited[i] != NULL) {
            struct Node* orig = queue[i];
            if (orig)
                for (int j = 0; j < orig->numNeighbors; j++)
                    visited[i]->neighbors[j] = visited[orig->neighbors[j]->val];
        }
    }

    return cloneStart;
}
```

### 🧠 Why it’s good
✅ No recursion  
✅ Easy to understand  
✅ Level-by-level traversal  

