### ✅ Correct Approach for “Minimum Height Trees” Problem

**Problem:** Given a tree with `n` nodes and edges, return all nodes which, when chosen as roots, produce minimum height trees.  

**Algorithm (Beginner-Friendly BFS Leaves Trimming):**

1. Build an **adjacency list** from edges.  
2. Initialize a list of **leaves** (nodes with only one neighbor).  
3. Iteratively **remove leaves** layer by layer until **1 or 2 nodes remain**.  
4. Remaining nodes are the **roots of Minimum Height Trees**.  

---

### ✅ Correct LeetCode-Style Implementation

```c
#include <stdlib.h>

int* findMinHeightTrees(int n, int** edges, int edgesSize, int* edgesColSize, int* returnSize){
    if(n == 1){
        int* ans = (int*)malloc(sizeof(int));
        ans[0] = 0;
        *returnSize = 1;
        return ans;
    }

    int** adj = (int**)malloc(n * sizeof(int*));
    int* adjSize = (int*)calloc(n, sizeof(int));
    for(int i = 0; i < n; i++) adj[i] = (int*)malloc(n * sizeof(int));

    for(int i = 0; i < edgesSize; i++){
        int u = edges[i][0], v = edges[i][1];
        adj[u][adjSize[u]++] = v;
        adj[v][adjSize[v]++] = u;
    }

    int* leaves = (int*)malloc(n * sizeof(int));
    int leavesCount = 0;
    for(int i = 0; i < n; i++){
        if(adjSize[i] == 1) leaves[leavesCount++] = i;
    }

    int remainingNodes = n;
    while(remainingNodes > 2){
        remainingNodes -= leavesCount;
        int* newLeaves = (int*)malloc(n * sizeof(int));
        int newCount = 0;

        for(int i = 0; i < leavesCount; i++){
            int leaf = leaves[i];
            for(int j = 0; j < adjSize[leaf]; j++){
                int neighbor = adj[leaf][j];
                // Remove leaf from neighbor's adjacency list
                for(int k = 0; k < adjSize[neighbor]; k++){
                    if(adj[neighbor][k] == leaf){
                        adj[neighbor][k] = adj[neighbor][adjSize[neighbor]-1];
                        adjSize[neighbor]--;
                        break;
                    }
                }
                if(adjSize[neighbor] == 1) newLeaves[newCount++] = neighbor;
            }
        }
        free(leaves);
        leaves = newLeaves;
        leavesCount = newCount;
    }

    int* result = (int*)malloc(leavesCount * sizeof(int));
    for(int i = 0; i < leavesCount; i++) result[i] = leaves[i];
    *returnSize = leavesCount;

    for(int i = 0; i < n; i++) free(adj[i]);
    free(adj);
    free(adjSize);
    free(leaves);

    return result;
}
```

